All six features are implemented and verified. Here's a summary of what changed:

**`app/auth.py`** — `require_api_key` now checks the `X-API-Key` header against `VALID_API_KEYS`; raises `401` if missing or invalid, returns the username on success.

**`app/main.py`** — Four endpoints modified/added:

- **`GET /tasks`** — Added optional query params `status`, `priority`, `assigned_to` (combinable filters) plus `page` (default 1) and `page_size` (default 20) for pagination.
- **`POST /tasks`** — Requires auth via `require_api_key`. Validates `project_id` against the projects list (404 if missing). Auto-generates a unique integer ID. Returns 201.
- **`PUT /tasks/{task_id}`** — Requires auth. Applies partial updates (only fields set in `TaskUpdate`). Returns 404 if task not found.
- **`DELETE /tasks/{task_id}`** — Requires auth. Removes and returns the task. Returns 404 if not found.

All endpoints were tested end-to-end — auth rejection (401), successful creation (201), project validation (404), partial update, deletion, combined filtering, and pagination all behave correctly.
